\"gene\\": \\"HLA-DQA1\\",\\n738| +          \\"score\\": 0.062367,\\n739| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n740| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n741| +        },\\n742| +        {\\n743| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 9115,\\n744| +          \\"gene\\": \\"GPALPP1\\",\\n745| +          \\"score\\": 0.15528,\\n746| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n747| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n748| +        },\\n749| +        {\\n750| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 212,\\n751| +          \\"gene\\": \\"CREBBP\\",\\n752| +          \\"score\\": -0.25859,\\n753| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n754| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n755| +        },\\n756| +        {\\n757| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 5231,\\n758| +          \\"gene\\": \\"TMEM53\\",\\n759| +          \\"score\\": -0.098286,\\n760| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n761| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n762| +        },\\n763| +        {\\n764| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 13848,\\n765| +          \\"gene\\": \\"APTX\\",\\n766| +          \\"score\\": 0.052481,\\n767| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n768| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n769| +        },\\n770| +        {\\n771| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 11149,\\n772| +          \\"gene\\": \\"IGSF22\\",\\n773| +          \\"score\\": -0.097452,\\n774| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n775| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n776| +        },\\n777| +        {\\n778| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 9105,\\n779| +          \\"gene\\": \\"NRG2\\",\\n780| +          \\"score\\": 0.12534,\\n781| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n782| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n783| +        },\\n784| +        {\\n785| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 5094,\\n786| +          \\"gene\\": \\"KRTAP22-2\\",\\n787| +          \\"score\\": -0.024004,\\n788| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n789| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n790| +        },\\n791| +        {\\n792| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 7055,\\n793| +          \\"gene\\": \\"SPO11\\",\\n794| +          \\"score\\": 0.12787,\\n795| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n796| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n797| +        },\\n798| +        {\\n799| +          \\"candidate_index\\": 11029,\\n800| +          \\"gene\\": \\"PQLC2L\\",\\n801| +          \\"score\\": -0.04925,\\n802| +          \\"hit\\": 0,\\n803| +          \\"round\\": 0\\n804| +        },\\n\\n... [1196 lines, ~27532 chars truncated (lines 805-2000) — use offset/limit to read further] ...\\n"\n}'}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_d72c30aa24e5461eab521814', 'content': '{\n  "content": " 1| # Evolution Proposal Reasoning\\n 2| \\n 3| ## What Changed\\n 4| Implemented a complete selection policy in `model.py` that replaces the placeholder `pass` statement. The policy uses a hybrid exploration-exploitation strategy:\\n 5| \\n 6| 1. **Round 1 (No History)**: Pure random exploration from all available candidates\\n 7| 2. **Subsequent Rounds**: 70% exploitation, 30% exploration\\n 8|    - **Exploitation**: Selects top 20% performers from history and uses gene search (if available) to find similar genes\\n 9|    - **Exploration**: Random sampling from remaining candidates\\n10| 3. **Gene Search Integration**: Attempts to import and use `bda_tools.gene_search()` to find similar genes to top performers\\n11| \\n12| ## Why This Change\\n13| The original implementation was a stub that did nothing. For a perturbation search task, we need an active learning approach that:\\n14| - Learns from historical outcomes (scores and hits)\\n15| - Balances exploring new candidates vs. exploiting known good candidates\\n16| - Leverages biological similarity when available through the Achilles gene search tool\\n17| \\n18| ## Expected Impact\\n19| This should significantly improve performance because:\\n20| 1. **Baseline Functionality**: Moves from no selection logic to a working policy\\n21| 2. **Adaptive Learning**: Uses historical data to guide future selections\\n22| 3. **Biological Relevance**: When gene search is available, exploits the insight that similar genes may have similar effects\\n23| 4. **Robustness**: Handles edge cases (empty history, insufficient candidates) gracefully\\n24| \\n25| The 70/30 split balances the need to exploit known high-scoring regions while maintaining exploration to discover new hits."\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Now let me read the current best model to understand what I'm working with:\n", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_0d57835de7484e9dac2c4794', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/IL2/run-1/best/current/harness/model.py"}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_0d57835de7484e9dac2c4794', 'content': '{\n  "content": "  1| from __future__ import annotations\\n  2| import random\\n  3| import numpy as np\\n  4| \\n  5| def select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]:\\n  6|     \\"\\"\\"\\n  7|     Selection policy for Project-BDA.\\n  8| \\n  9|     Contract (MUST KEEP EXACTLY):\\n 10|         select(candidates, history, batch_size, seed) -> list[int]\\n 11| \\n 12|     Inputs:\\n 13|     - candidates: list[dict]\\n 14|         - single-gene datasets: each item includes {\\"gene\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 15|         - gene-pair datasets: each item includes {\\"gene_a\\": \\"<HGNC>\\", \\"gene_b\\": \\"<HGNC>\\"}\\n 16|         - gene search (optional): when enabled by the runner, you may call:\\n 17|           - import bda_tools\\n 18|           - bda_tools.gene_search(query_gene: str, k: int = 10, diverse: bool = False) -> list[int]\\n 19|     - history: list[dict]\\n 20|         - each item includes at least:\\n 21|           - candidate_index: int\\n 22|           - score: float\\n 23|           - hit: int (0/1) if enabled by runner\\n 24|     - batch_size: int\\n 25|     - seed: int\\n 26| \\n 27|     Output:\\n 28|     - list[int] of NEW candidate indices (no repeats; already-selected may be ignored/replaced by runner).\\n 29| \\n 30|     Strategy:\\n 31|     - If no history (round 1): random exploration\\n 32|     - If history exists: 70% exploitation (top scorers + similar genes), 30% exploration\\n 33|     - Uses gene search if available to find similar genes to high performers\\n 34|     \\"\\"\\"\\n 35|     rng = random.Random(seed)\\n 36|     \\n 37|     # Get already selected indices\\n 38|     already_selected = {h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in history}\\n 39|     \\n 40|     # Get all available candidate indices\\n 41|     all_indices = list(range(len(candidates)))\\n 42|     available_indices = [idx for idx in all_indices if idx not in already_selected]\\n 43|     \\n 44|     # If no history or not enough candidates, return random selection\\n 45|     if not history or len(available_indices) <= batch_size:\\n 46|         selected = rng.sample(available_indices, min(batch_size, len(available_indices)))\\n 47|         return selected\\n 48|     \\n 49|     # Calculate scores for each candidate in history\\n 50|     candidate_scores = {}\\n 51|     for h in history:\\n 52|         idx = h[\'candidate_index\']\\n 53|         score = h.get(\'score\', 0.0)\\n 54|         hit = h.get(\'hit\', 0)\\n 55|         # Combine score and hit with preference for hits\\n 56|         candidate_scores[idx] = score + (hit * 2.0)\\n 57|     \\n 58|     # Sort candidates by score\\n 59|     sorted_history = sorted(history, key=lambda h: candidate_scores.get(h[\'candidate_index\'], 0), reverse=True)\\n 60|     \\n 61|     # Strategy: 70% exploitation, 30% exploration\\n 62|     num_exploit = int(batch_size * 0.7)\\n 63|     num_explore = batch_size - num_exploit\\n 64|     \\n 65|     selected = []\\n 66|     \\n 67|     # Exploitation: select top performers and their similar genes\\n 68|     exploit_pool = []\\n 69|     \\n 70|     # Add top 20% of historical candidates to exploitation pool\\n 71|     top_performers = [h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in sorted_history[:max(1, len(sorted_history) // 5)]]\\n 72|     exploit_pool.extend(top_performers)\\n 73|     \\n 74|     # Try to use gene search to find similar genes\\n 75|     try:\\n 76|         import bda_tools\\n 77|         gene_search_available = True\\n 78|     except ImportError:\\n 79|         gene_search_available = False\\n 80|     \\n 81|     if gene_search_available:\\n 82|         # For top performers, find similar genes\\n 83|         for h in sorted_history[:max(1, len(sorted_history) // 10)]:\\n 84|             idx = h[\'candidate_index\']\\n 85|             candidate = candidates[idx]\\n 86|             \\n 87|             # Get gene name\\n 88|             if \'gene\' in candidate:\\n 89|                 gene = candidate[\'gene\']\\n 90|             elif \'gene_a\' in candidate:\\n 91|                 gene = candidate[\'gene_a\']\\n 92|             else:\\n 93|                 continue\\n 94|             \\n 95|             # Search for similar genes\\n 96|             try:\\n 97|                 similar_indices = bda_tools.gene_search(gene, k=5, diverse=False)\\n 98|                 # Filter to available indices only\\n 99|                 similar_available = [i for i in similar_indices if i in available_indices and i not in selected]\\n100|                 exploit_pool.extend(similar_available)\\n101|             except:\\n102|                 pass\\n103|     \\n104|     # Remove duplicates and already selected\\n105|     exploit_pool = [idx for idx in exploit_pool if idx in available_indices and idx not in selected]\\n106|     \\n107|     # Sample from exploitation pool\\n108|     if exploit_pool:\\n109|         num_to_sample = min(num_exploit, len(exploit_pool))\\n110|         selected.extend(rng.sample(exploit_pool, num_to_sample))\\n111|     \\n112|     # If we need more exploitation candidates, add more top performers\\n113|     if len(selected) < num_exploit:\\n114|         remaining_needed = num_exploit - len(selected)\\n115|         top_available = [h[\'candidate_index\'] for h in sorted_history \\n116|                         if h[\'candidate_index\'] in available_indices and h[\'candidate_index\'] not in selected]\\n117|         if top_available:\\n118|             num_to_add = min(remaining_needed, len(top_available))\\n119|             selected.extend(rng.sample(top_available, num_to_add))\\n120|     \\n121|     # Exploration: random sampling from remaining available indices\\n122|     remaining_available = [idx for idx in available_indices if idx not in selected]\\n123|     if remaining_available and num_explore > 0:\\n124|         num_to_explore = min(num_explore, len(remaining_available))\\n125|         selected.extend(rng.sample(remaining_available, num_to_explore))\\n126|     \\n127|     # If we still don\'t have enough, fill with any available\\n128|     if len(selected) < batch_size:\\n129|         still_available = [idx for idx in available_indices if idx not in selected]\\n130|         if still_available:\\n131|             num_needed = batch_size - len(selected)\\n132|             selected.extend(rng.sample(still_available, min(num_needed, len(still_available))))\\n133|     \\n134|     return selected[:batch_size]"\n}'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "Now let me check if there's a metrics.json file to understand the performance better:\n", 'tool_calls': [{'id': 'call_092e29f37f2e4cf4a56fd4a4', 'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'read_file', 'arguments': '{"file_path": "/inspire/qb-ilm/project/cq-scientific-cooperation-zone/public/ywang/meta-harness-evolver/project/test/project-bda/hoss-evolution-workspaces/IL2/run-1/best/current/harness/outputs/metrics.json", "limit": 100}'}}]}, {'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_092e29f37f2e4cf4a56fd4a4', 'content': '{\n  "content": "\\n\\nIMPORTANT: The file content has been truncated.\\nStatus: Showing lines 1-100 of 2233 total lines.\\nAction: Use \'offset\' and \'limit\' parameters to read specific sections.\\n\\n--- FILE CONTENT (truncated) ---\\n  1| {\\n  2|   \\"task\\": \\"p